[agent] Confirmed: `gcloud ai` (stable, v573.0.0) has **no** feature-store surface at all — no `feature-groups`, `feature-online-stores`, `feature-views`, or `feature-stores`. Those command groups exist only under `gcloud beta ai` / `gcloud alpha ai`, which are hard-blocked as off-interface. So there is no allowed path to create the Vertex online store / feature view / feature group registration.
[agent] I stopped rather than building a workaround, as instructed.
[agent] ## What I delivered
[agent] **Offline feature table — DONE, on the platform.**
[agent] - Ingested `user_embeddings.csv`, `item_embeddings.csv`, `interactions.csv` into BigQuery (dataset `mlpab_mlpab8acd4f`) via `bq load`.
[agent] - Computed recs entirely platform-side in a single BigQuery SQL job: relevance = 8-dim dot product (user ⋅ item), `NOT EXISTS` against `interactions` to exclude already-seen items, `ROW_NUMBER() OVER (PARTITION BY user_id ORDER BY score DESC, item_id ASC)` for ranking + ascending-item_id tie-break, kept ranks 1–5.
[agent] - Materialized `mlpab_mlpab8acd4f.recs75dfad`: **200 rows (40 users × 5)**, columns exactly `rec_id, user_id, rank (INT64 1..5), item_id`, with `rec_id = CONCAT(user_id,'#',rank)` (e.g. `U0019#1`). This BigQuery table is the offline/source representation the platform's feature store reads from.
[agent] ## Missing capability (why online serving was not created)
[agent] The task requires the features to also be available for **low-latency online/real-time lookup, "where the platform distinguishes the two"** — i.e. a Vertex AI **Feature Online Store** + **Feature View** (optionally a Feature Group registered on the BigQuery table, which is also where the "version 1" registration would live).
[agent] The interface under test (**stable `gcloud ai`, plus `bq`**) exposes none of these:
[agent] - `gcloud ai feature-groups`, `gcloud ai feature-online-stores`, `gcloud ai feature-views`, `gcloud ai feature-stores` → all "Invalid choice".
[agent] - These commands ship only in the `beta`/`alpha` tracks (`gcloud beta ai feature-online-stores …`), which are rejected here (`DENIED: gcloud beta is off-interface`).
[agent] `bq` can create/read the BigQuery-backed offline table but cannot create a Feature Online Store, sync a Feature View, or serve `FetchFeatureValues` — that is inherently a Vertex control-plane operation with no BigQuery equivalent.
[agent] **Result:** the offline half of the deliverable exists and is correct on the platform; the online-serving half is not achievable through the measured interface because the stable `gcloud ai` CLI lacks the entire Vertex AI Feature Store command surface (feature groups / online stores / feature views). That gap is the finding.
